CLAUDE.md
# Docs are local working notes and stay untracked — except performance/, which holds the
# baseline measurements Phases 1-3 of the performance plan are graded against. A
# before/after record is worthless if it only exists on one machine.
#
# Written as `/docs/*` rather than `/docs` on purpose: git never descends into a fully
# excluded directory, so a negation nested inside one can never take effect.
/docs/*
!/docs/performance/
.mobile-agents/
/mockups
.DS_Store

